<p>Ukrainian drones struck the Tuapse oil refinery on Russia’s Black Sea coast overnight on April 28, sparking another large fire and evacuations near the Rosneft-owned facility in Krasnodar Krai, Russian regional authorities said. The latest strike followed earlier April attacks that left fires burning for days at Tuapse oil infrastructure. Krasnodar officials said the latest blaze started after drone debris fell on the refinery grounds and reported no casualties. Ukraine’s Unmanned Systems Forces later said it carried out the operation, according to NV, while Kremlin spokesman Dmitry Peskov accused Kyiv of worsening strains on global energy markets.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ERn0t3Puqh3WIfssK5C9oMgxFw3UEtnLFV5PVmKXvgTbqYE1lZO9W8CeSLJgFtglV1hP9vFJHh75QklfboRN5_-m0i8cufT1lmmPzfO8_2gLjM26kgJNosbz2ujcY6MVdai3IPgeMy-aivdBEz7vNo8nEhQ' alt='Smoke rises after a fire at the Tuapse oil refinery following a reported Ukrainian drone strike.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Fire response: Emergency crews initially deployed 122 personnel and 39 pieces of equipment, while Krasnodar Governor Veniamin Kondratyev later said 164 people and 46 vehicles were involved.</li><li>Federal response: Reports said Russian President Vladimir Putin ordered Emergency Situations Minister Alexander Kurenkov to travel to Tuapse as the response continued.</li><li>Environmental damage: After the April 20 attack, oil products entered the Black Sea and formed a slick covering 10,000 square meters, with residents later reporting oily rain in Tuapse.</li></ul><blockquote>The Kiev regime has once again struck oil storage facilities, where the oil was intended for export operations, that is, for fulfilling export contract obligations - Dmitry Peskov</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Krasnodar regional authorities: Governor Veniamin Kondratyev called the refinery fire a serious emergency and said the firefighting force would be expanded. (<a href='https://energy-policy.ru/tuapsinskij-npz-snova-gorit/novosti/2026/04/28/'>Energy Policy</a>)</li><li>Kremlin: Dmitry Peskov said President Vladimir Putin had been briefed on Tuapse and that federal response measures were underway. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639210-ukraine-attacks-refinery-global-oil-suply/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Ukraine’s Unmanned Systems Forces: The force described the refinery as linked to Moscow’s war machine and released footage of the operation. (<a href='https://english.nv.ua/nation/ukraine-confirms-third-strike-in-a-month-on-russia-s-tuapse-oil-refinery-50603708.html'>NV</a>)</li><li>Local residents and independent Russian media: Residents described hours of drone activity, heavy smoke and the smell of burning, while the environmental outlet Kedr said huge black plumes again hung over the city. (<a href='https://novayagazeta.eu/articles/2026/04/28/ukraina-povtorno-atakovala-npz-v-tuapse-news'>Novaya Gazeta Europe</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.reddit.com/r/worldnews/comments/1sxvzmm/ukraine_hammers_russian_black_sea_oil_facilities/'>Ukraine hammers Russian Black Sea oil facilities</a> - reddit.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rferl.org/a/tuapse-russian-oil-port-fire-drone-strike/33744191.html'>Russian Black Sea Oil Facility On Fire Again After Ukrainian Strike</a> - rferl.org</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/cvgzd4qk7qgo'>Third Ukrainian strike hits Russian oil refinery and prompts evacuations</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://meduza.io/en/news/2026/04/28/drone-debris-strikes-russian-oil-refinery-prompting-evacuation-of-nearby-residents'>Drone debris sparks fire at Russian oil refinery, prompting evacuation of nearby residents</a> - meduza.io</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/russia/639210-ukraine-attacks-refinery-global-oil-suply/'>Kiev’s attacks on Russian refinery cutting global oil supply – Kremlin</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3351733/ukrainian-drone-attack